Package: TEfastR
Title: Fast, Vectorized Gene/Transposable Element Read Counting
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Sulev", "Koks", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "sulevkoks@gmail.com")
Description: A vectorized, Bioconductor-based reimplementation of the
    read-counting stage of TEtranscripts (Jin et al. 2015)
    <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btv422>. Counts reads/fragments in a BAM
    file against gene and transposable element (TE) annotations, using
    bulk GenomicRanges overlap operations instead of a per-alignment loop,
    and a sparse-matrix SQUAREM EM algorithm to redistribute multi-mapped
    reads across TE instances. Produces the same gene/TE count table used
    by TEtranscripts' downstream DESeq2-based differential expression
    step. See the package vignette for a user guide and known differences
    from the Python TEtranscripts implementation.
